## Initial Setup

### Quick Start
git remote -v             # which remote repositories are you connected to? 
git init                  # initialize a new .git folder which will allow you to track local commits
git remote add origin <url>   # add a new remote repo
git branch -M <name>        # rename the branch

> make sure you create your .gitignore <

Example:
--------------------------
# Visual Studio
.vs/

# .NET build files
bin/
obj/

# User-specific Visual Studio files
*.user
*.suo
-----------------------------

git add .             # add all untracked files, or specific directories thru .\example\
git status            # verify changes to be committed
git commit -m "example"   # your commit message
git push -u origin <name>  # push changes
git branch                 # view what branch you are on
git switch -c <name>      # create a new branch and switch to it
git switch <name>          # switch to a new branch
git branch -d <name>       # remove branch 

-------------------------------------------------------------------------

git restore --staged .            # if you accidentally run git add . and stage like 30+ files you didn't mean to
git fetch origin                  # pull updates without merging


